          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %em Frobenius morphism
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
            acting on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras"} algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras"} function algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaves"} structure sheaves
            etc., which takes each
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "-element" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            to its
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi x
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi factors
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x^p = \underbrace{x \cdot x \cdots x}_{p \; factors}
                  \\;.
          %p
            It is precisely in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+characteristic"} positive characteristic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            that this operation is indeed an algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/freshman+dream+arithmetic"}> freshman dream arithmetic
            ”).
          %p
            The Frobenius map is the shadow of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, remark 2.2.7
            ).
          %p
            The presence of the Frobenius endomorphism in characteristic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is a fundamental property in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            that controls many of its deep aspects. Notably
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+functions"} zeta functions
            are typically expressed in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the Frobenius endomorphisms on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
            and so it features prominently for instance in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+conjectures"} Weil conjectures
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borger%27s+absolute+geometry"} Borger's absolute geometry
            lifts of Frobenius endomorphisms through
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            for all primes at once – in the sense of
            %em
              %a{:href => "Lambda-ring#LambdaRingByFrobeniusLifts"} Lambda-ring structure
            – is interpreted as encoding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            data from traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spec%28Z%29"} Spec(Z)
            down to the “absolute” geometry over “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1"}> F1
            ”. See at
            %em
              %a{:href => "Borger%27s+absolute+geometry#Motivation"} Borger’s absolute geometry – Motivation
            for more on this.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %blockquote
            %p this entry may need attention
          %h2#for_fields For fields
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of positive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %strong Frobenius morphism
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
            of the field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon k \to k
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F(a) \coloneqq  a^p
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that this is indeed a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of fields: the identity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a b)^p=a^p b^p
            evidently holds for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b\in k
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            of the field is used to show
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a+b)^p=a^p+b^p
          %h3#of_schemes Of schemes
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{O}_X)
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %strong absolute Frobenius
            is the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi ab
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{ab}:(X,\mathcal{O}_X)\to (X,\mathcal{O}_X)
            which is the identity on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and on the structure sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_*:\mathcal{O}_X\to \mathcal{O}_X
            is the
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-schemes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as an
            = succeed "-scheme," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi ab
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi ab
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\displaystyle \begin{matrix} X &amp; \stackrel{F^{ab}}{\to} &amp; X \\
                  \\downarrow &amp;  &amp; \downarrow \\
                  S &amp; \stackrel{F^{ab}}{\to} &amp; S \end{matrix}
            ,
          %p
            so in order for the map to be an
            = succeed "-scheme" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{ab}
            must be the identity on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S=Spec(\mathbb{F}_p)
          %p
            Now we can form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            using this square:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi S
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(p)}:=X\times_{S} S
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi rel
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{rel}:X\to X^{(p)}
            so that the composition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X^{(p)}\to X
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{ab}
            = succeed "." do
              %strong relative Frobenius
            = succeed "-schemes." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h3#for_sheaves_on_
            For sheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C Ring ^{op}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            be a prime number, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a field of characteristic
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            we define
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
