              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
              the Frobenius homomorphism from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EInfinityFrobenius"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi H
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H A \longrightarrow H A^{t C_p}
            %p
              coincides on the 0th
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+group"} stable homotopy group
              with the ordinary Frobenius homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \longrightarrow A/p
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"}> Nikolaus-Scholze 17, example IV.1.1
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#for_rings_2 For rings
          %ul
            %li
              The Frobenius homomorphism is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Frob
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ring
                          %mi p
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ring
                          %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Frob_p\colon Id_{Ring_p}\Rightarrow Id_{Ring_p}
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
              containing all rings with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              to itself.
          %h3#for_fields_2 For fields
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The Frobenius morphism on algebras is always
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective"} injective
                %em not
                always a monomorphism.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                of the Frobenius morphism is the set of elements of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                with a
                = succeed "-th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^{1/p}
            %li
              %p
                The Frobenius morphism is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective"} surjective
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect
          %h3#AsElementsOfGaloisGroup As elements of the Galois group
          %p
            Some powers of the Frobenius morphism canonically induce elements in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
            (…)
          %p
            Review of the standard story is for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Snyder02"}> Snyder 02, section 1.5
            ). Further developments include (
            %a{:href => "#DokchitserDokchitser10"}> Dokchitser-Dokchitser 10
            )
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_{p^n}
            is a
            = succeed ",then" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+field"} finite field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(\mathbb{F}_{p^n}/\mathbb{F}_p)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
            by the Frobenius map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\mapsto x^p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Snyder02"} Snyder 02, lemma 1.5.10
          %p (..)
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+L-function"} Artin L-function
          %h3#for_schemes For schemes
          %p
            For the purposes below
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            will be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            = succeed ">" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_*\mathcal{O}_X
                is a free
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                by studying properties of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_*\mathcal{O}_X
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+scheme"} proper
                over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi F
                            %mi ab
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to \mathcal{O}_X\stackrel{F^{ab}}{\to} F_*\mathcal{O}_X \to d\mathcal{O}_X\to 0
                is exact and if it
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequence"} splits
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                has a lifting to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_2(k)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "-formal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+algebraic+scheme"} locally algebraic scheme
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+scheme"} étale
              iff the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphism"} Frobenius morphism
              = succeed "is" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_X:X\to X^{(p)}
          %p The Frobenius as a morphism (natural transformation) of (affine) group schemes is one operation among other (related) operations of interest:
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              For any commutative affine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              the Frobenius- and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verschiebung+morphism"} Verschiebung morphism
              correspond by “completed
              = succeed "\u2019\u2019;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartier+duality"} Cartier duality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat D(V_G)=F_{\hat D(G)}
          %p
            For a more detailed account of the relationship of Frobenius-,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verschiebung+morphism"} Verschiebung-
            and
            %span.newWikiWord
              homothety morphism
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/homothety+morphism"} ?
            see
            %a{:href => "#Hazewinkel"} Hazewinkel
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin-Schreier+sequence"} Artin-Schreier sequence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+conjecture"} Weil conjecture
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+Lie+algebra"} restricted Lie algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shtuka"} shtuka
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclotomic+spectrum"} cyclotomic spectrum
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Frobenius68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ferdinand+Georg+Frobenius"}> Ferdinand Georg Frobenius
              , Vol 2, around p. 719 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gesammelte Abhandlungen
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%BCnter+Tamme"}> Günter Tamme
                , section II 4.2 of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+%C3%89tale+Cohomology"} Introduction to Étale Cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
                , section 27 of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+%C3%89tale+Cohomology"} Lectures on Étale Cohomology
          %p
            Further discussion of the relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Snyder02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noah+Snyder"}> Noah Snyder
                , section 1.5 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Artin L-Functions: A Historical Approach
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.columbia.edu/~nsnyder/thesismain.pdf"} pdf
            %li#DokchitserDokchitser10
              %p
                Tim Dokchitser, Vladimir Dokchitser,
                %em Identifying Frobenius elements in Galois groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.5388"}> arXiv:1009.5388
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Michel Demazure,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lectures+on+p-divisible+groups"} lectures on p-divisible groups
                %a{:href => "http://sites.google.com/site/mtnpdivisblegroupsworkshop/lecture-notes-on-p-divisible-groups"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michiel+Hazewinkel"}> Michiel Hazewinkel
                , witt vectors. part 1,
                %a#Hazewinkel{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0804.3888v1"} arXiv:0804.3888v1
            %li
              %p
                Karen Smith,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Brief Guide to Some of the Literature on F-singularities
                %a{:href => "www.aimath.org/WWN/singularvariety/F-sings.pdf"} American Institute of Mathematics
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+rings"} E-infinity rings
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rational+and+p-adic+Homotopy+Theory"} Rational and p-adic Homotopy Theory
          %p
            Discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+rings"} E-infinity rings
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+spectra"} Tate spectra
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#NikolausScholze17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Scholze"} Peter Scholze
              %em On topological cyclic homology
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.01799"}> arXiv:1707.01799
              )
          %p A brief discussion in the context of algebraic geometry over rigs is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              %em Core Varieties, Extensivity, and Rig Geometry
              , TAC
              %strong 20
              no.14 (2008) pp.497-503. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/20/14/20-14abs.html"}> abstract
              )
